# Example sudoers grant for scripts/host-ops/pin-prod-sha (gr685985).
#
# Installed BY HAND on the session-MCP host(s) with visudo — no script
# installs it. <worker user> is the factory's deploy user; <owner> is the
# user that owns the prod watched checkout; the helper path must be the
# absolute path on the host (the checkout that holds the repo, not a
# repo-relative one). The grant names this one script only: sudo runs it
# with a scrubbed environment, it takes no env and no arguments but the
# sha, and it does only the pin.
<worker user> ALL=(<owner>) NOPASSWD: <absolute helper path>
